{
  "_comment": "Reviewed mapping for competitors' own benchmarks. Leak/FP bytes are class-agnostic; these tables only drive the typed-entity metrics and the common-intersection view. `gold` maps each benchmark's native gold label to canonical labels (the 25 main-corpus labels plus the `extension_labels`). `tool_extension` adds canonical labels that a tool label covers but that the main corpus never annotates, so compare/label-map.json maps it to nothing or to a narrower label. The composed tool-label -> native-gold-label table is derived from both, never written by hand. `gold['pii-trace']` follows the dataset card and the paper's Table 6: account_number covers only the named national ID, SSN, IBAN, card, sort code and generic id-number types; other_pii is a residual bucket with no stated class and maps to nothing. `native_gold` is the identity map for a tool whose native labels are the benchmark's own labels (PII-Tracer on PII-TRACE); it replaces the canonical composition for that pair only.",
